---
// Concepts › Architecture: where sources and built archives travel during
// `vorpal build` (docs-redesign step 6). Every file goes through the
// registry: the agent daemon pushes sources (cli/src/command/start/agent.rs,
// push), the worker pulls them and pushes the built archive
// (start/worker.rs:293-312), and the CLI pulls archives
// (cli/src/command/build.rs:137, pull_archive). The CLI's only call to the
// worker is the build request, whose reply is the build's log lines
// (build.rs:290, build_artifact).
import Diagram from '../Diagram.astro';
---

<Diagram
	title="Sources and built archives go through the registry; the CLI sends the worker only build requests"
	width={680}
	height={318}
	marker="dg-flow-ah"
>
	<rect class="vp-dg-box" x="10" y="10" width="170" height="60" rx="8"></rect>
	<text class="vp-dg-t" x="28" y="36">Config program</text>
	<text class="vp-dg-s" x="28" y="57">your SDK code</text>

	<rect class="vp-dg-box" x="270" y="10" width="200" height="60" rx="8"></rect>
	<text class="vp-dg-t" x="288" y="36">Agent daemon</text>
	<text class="vp-dg-s" x="288" y="57">pins and pushes sources</text>

	<rect class="vp-dg-box hot" x="10" y="130" width="170" height="60" rx="8"></rect>
	<text class="vp-dg-t" x="28" y="156">CLI</text>
	<text class="vp-dg-m" x="28" y="177">vorpal build</text>

	<rect class="vp-dg-box" x="500" y="130" width="170" height="60" rx="8"></rect>
	<text class="vp-dg-t" x="518" y="156">Registry</text>
	<text class="vp-dg-s" x="518" y="177">sources and archives</text>

	<rect class="vp-dg-box" x="270" y="248" width="200" height="60" rx="8"></rect>
	<text class="vp-dg-t" x="288" y="274">Worker</text>
	<text class="vp-dg-s" x="288" y="295">runs the steps</text>

	<path class="vp-dg-l" d="M95 130 V74" marker-end="url(#dg-flow-ah)"></path>
	<text class="vp-dg-s" x="103" y="106">starts</text>

	<path class="vp-dg-l" d="M180 40 H266" marker-end="url(#dg-flow-ah)"></path>
	<text class="vp-dg-s" x="186" y="32">declares</text>

	<path class="vp-dg-l hot" d="M470 40 C560 40 585 80 585 126" marker-end="url(#dg-flow-ah)"></path>
	<text class="vp-dg-s" x="596" y="84">sources</text>

	<path class="vp-dg-l hot" d="M500 160 H184" marker-end="url(#dg-flow-ah)"></path>
	<text class="vp-dg-s" x="262" y="152">archives, pulled by the CLI</text>

	<path class="vp-dg-l hot" d="M470 278 C560 278 585 236 585 194" marker-start="url(#dg-flow-ah)" marker-end="url(#dg-flow-ah)"></path>
	<text class="vp-dg-s" x="480" y="306">pull and push</text>

	<path class="vp-dg-l vp-dg-req" d="M95 190 C95 250 180 278 266 278" marker-end="url(#dg-flow-ah)"></path>
	<text class="vp-dg-s" x="40" y="290">build request</text>

	<Fragment slot="words">
		<li>
			The CLI builds your config program and starts it. The config program declares each
			artifact to the agent daemon.
		</li>
		<li>
			The agent daemon checks each source against <code>Vorpal.lock</code>, hashes it, and pushes
			it to the registry.
		</li>
		<li>
			For each artifact, the CLI looks in its local store, then pulls the built archive from the
			registry if the registry has it.
		</li>
		<li>
			For an artifact neither has, the CLI sends the worker a build request and shows the build's
			log lines. The worker pulls the sources and dependency outputs from the registry, runs the
			steps, and pushes the archive to the registry, where the CLI pulls it.
		</li>
		<li>No source or archive passes between the CLI and the worker; every file goes through the registry.</li>
	</Fragment>
</Diagram>
